              "id": "B1DMfB",
              "name": "Text",
              "fill": "#15171C",
              "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
              "width": "fill_container",
              "content": "The app's files, database, queue, secrets and cache moved from AWS (simulated) to Leaseweb in Amsterdam (NL) with nothing lost: every count matches and every checksum is equal. After the move, the attacker agent found PostgreSQL 5432 open to the Internet. The defense agent closed it with a person's approval in Telegram; it was exposed for 36 s. The rule that caused it is fixed in code (PR #1), and the action can be undone.",
              "lineHeight": 1.5,
              "fontFamily": "$sans",
              "fontSize": 18,
              "fontWeight": "normal"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "frame",
